      "answer": "Based on the source code, here's how the universe of a set image is chosen:\n\n**Function:** `_image_universe` at `source/lib/_magma.py:1967-1989`\n\n**For structural codomains:**\n- The structural codomain **itself is the universe**, even for empty images (line 1970)\n- Supported structural codomains include those satisfying `_is_struct()` or being `_MFinField`, `_MResRing`, or `_MFFPolyRing` (line 1977)\n\n**For set codomains:**\n- **Nonempty images:** Uses the set's declared universe if one is supplied; if unsupported, returns None. If no declared universe, inference is attempted (integer/rational only) (lines 1980-1988)\n- **Empty images:** The source code states (lines 1973-1975) that \"An empty image into a set would have that set itself as its universe in Magma. Sagebrush cannot represent this and refuses it.\" Empty images into structural codomains are still allowed\n\nThe logic is implemented in `_image_universe` (returning the universe or None) and enforced in `_map_set_image` at line 2001, which calls `_image_universe(mapping.cod, not images)` where the second parameter indicates whether the image is empty.",
